    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d910">

                <pb facs="0947" n="939" xml:id="pg939"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.6176/69</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1035</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-22">August 22, 1938</date>.<lb/>[Received August
                        30.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to despatch No.
                    159 of April 7, 1938,<anchor n="15" xml:id="d910-f1"/> and subsequent
                    correspondence regarding the International Rubber Regulation Draft Agreement and
                    to report that Sir John Campbell, Chairman of the International Rubber
                    Regulation Committee, made a public announcement on the evening of August 9 that
                    the contracting Governments had signified their intention of accepting the Draft
                    Agreement which will come into effect on January 1 next for a period of five
                    years.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herschel V.
                    Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
